.DS_Store
__pycache__/

# Tooling scratch
.playwright-mcp/
*.bak

# This repository holds the skill only: rule prose, design tokens, entry points,
# and the check scripts. Deliverables produced *with* the skill — decks, reports,
# their exports and renders — live with the engagement, never here. Committing one
# would also breach the no-engagement-facts red line in CLAUDE.md.
*.pdf
*.pptx
*.docx
*.key
*.numbers
*.xlsx
*.mp4
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.webp
*.svg
*.woff
*.woff2
*.ttf
*.otf

# Skill-validation output. Deliverables built to exercise the rules used to land
# in docs/ so they could be checked in place; they carry engagement facts and a
# client name, which CLAUDE.md red line 9 bars from this repository. As of
# 0.1.385 they land in the user's own Documents/LUMI-Style/ like every other
# deliverable, so red line 9 is held by the directory structure rather than by
# this file. The entry stays as a net: a rule enforced only by .gitignore is one
# `git add -f` away from being broken, and the directory is the one place a
# validation run has historically reached for.
docs/

# Exception: the design language's own assets are part of the skill, not renders.
# design-rules.md requires embedding them, and a version that shipped with the
# face declared but not vendored rendered nothing (CHANGELOG 1.2.0). The icons
# and geography added in 1.8.0 sit behind the same blanket *.svg rule and would
# have been dropped the same silent way.
!assets/fonts/*.woff2
!assets/icons/**/*.svg
!assets/vectors/*.svg
# LUMIVATE's brand marks. Generated, locked, and shipped — the blanket
# *.svg above is there to keep stray artwork out, not the package's own
# generated vectors, and this is the fourth directory to need saying so.
!assets/brand/**/*.svg
# The shape library, and the fifth directory to need saying so — which is why
# the saying is now a guard. All 206 units sat here untracked from extraction
# until 0.1.496: on disk for every local check, absent from every clone. The
# `assets tracked` guard in check_repo.py asks git rather than the filesystem,
# so a sixth directory cannot be forgotten this quietly.
!assets/shapes/*.svg
# Official platform marks for the get-started page; provenance in SOURCES.md.
!assets/logos/*.svg
# The model-family marks live one level down, and the blanket *.svg rule above
# reaches them: without this the twenty-three logos p4 draws would be on disk,
# green in every check, and absent from the package. Same trap the Microsoft
# raster hit at 0.1.521.
!assets/logos/models/*.svg
# A raster mark, where its owner publishes no vector from its own domains.
# Scoped to this directory: the blanket *.png rule exists so an engagement
# screenshot cannot be committed, and that reason does not reach a vendored
# trademark whose provenance is recorded beside it.
!assets/logos/*.png
!assets/logos/SOURCES.md

# Conformance run artifacts: renders, not records. The scoreboard is tracked;
# the raw agent output lives with the run.
conformance/results/

# inspect_layout contact sheets are renders, not records.
fixtures/_layout/

# inspect_layout contact sheets are renders, not records — the same reason
# fixtures/_layout is ignored.
backlog/_layout/
# A rendered deck slipped in as backlog/ideas-prd.en.html once (deleted at
# 0.1.436): *.html was never in this list, so the deliverable ban had a hole.
backlog/*.html

# Claude Code worktrees: separate checkouts, not content of this one.
.claude/worktrees/

# The Evals corpus paths are the operator machine's, not the package's
# (red line 9: no engagement facts in a tracked file).
evals/corpus.local.json
evals/measured.local.json
# The board's price table: tokens ship in traces, prices are one operator
# machine's dated fact, and a committed price is a stored derivation waiting
# to go stale (the reason cost_usd left the trace schema).
evals/prices.local.json
# Third-party study decks: never committed (copyright; study only — see SOURCES.md)
references/exemplars/external/*.pdf

# The out-of-bounds lists (check_privacy.py --terms; OR-8). Their home is
# ~/.lumi/terms/, outside every checkout, and this net is the second layer:
# a list copied beside a deliverable for convenience must still never be
# added. A rule enforced only by a directory convention is one `cp` away from
# being broken, and this file says the same thing about docs/ above.
*.terms.txt
terms-oob*
